  "source": "Trinity Energy Systems, EMPOWER-PLUS Operational Manual, document version 4.0 (2019-06-27)",
  "notes": [
    "Modbus RTU on RS-485, 9600 8N1, function 03 only; the station ID is set on the meter. A read of more than 254 bytes, or from an address that does not exist, returns exception 02.",
    "Addresses are the decimal numbers of the manual (200 is the first); they are written here as printed, address base 1. Values are unsigned: 32-bit (two registers) up to 308 and 16-bit from 310 on, each with the manual's multiplication factor (100 for most, 1000 for the power factors, 1 for time values).",
    "The first 50 registers of the earlier unofficial EM9400 map from the Modbus Database have the same addresses and names as this manual, so the EM9400 is taken to be the same meter; the manual itself calls the product EMPOWER-PLUS.",
    "The word order of the 32-bit values is not stated; high word first is assumed.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual; not tested on a device."
  ],
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "big",
  "address_base": 1,
  "x_status": "official",
